WEBVTT

00:00:00.043 --> 00:00:01.044 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Builder.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.784 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Blueprint.

00:00:03.349 --> 00:00:04.113 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson two.

00:00:04.633 --> 00:00:06.141 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
What you are going to need.

00:00:06.952 --> 00:00:08.098 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Education only.

00:00:08.657 --> 00:00:09.971 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Not financial advice.

00:00:10.491 --> 00:00:12.314 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information

00:00:12.314 --> 00:00:14.746 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and doesn't consider your objectives,

00:00:14.746 --> 00:00:16.646 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
financial situation or needs.

00:00:17.166 --> 00:00:18.930 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is high risk; you could

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.621 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lose all the money you put in.

00:00:21.141 --> 00:00:23.192 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Past performance is not a reliable

00:00:23.192 --> 00:00:24.890 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
indicator of future results.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.549 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A daily close is the last

00:00:27.549 --> 00:00:28.555 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price of that day.

00:00:29.055 --> 00:00:31.111 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The prices are public historical

00:00:31.111 --> 00:00:32.873 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
daily closes, marked Example.

00:00:34.073 --> 00:00:35.973 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No order is sent from this lesson.

00:00:36.971 --> 00:00:39.785 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is a digital coin, such as bitcoin.

00:00:40.305 --> 00:00:42.439 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A range is the top and the bottom,

00:00:42.439 --> 00:00:44.819 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap is the space between two lines,

00:00:44.819 --> 00:00:47.117 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the step is how wide that gap is.

00:00:47.637 --> 00:00:49.676 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stop is the rule for what you will

00:00:49.676 --> 00:00:51.568 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
do if the price leaves the range.

00:00:52.088 --> 00:00:53.988 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Like a packing list before a trip,

00:00:53.988 --> 00:00:55.887 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your page comes before any screen.

00:00:56.812 --> 00:00:58.320 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
By the end you will fill in

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.259 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a seven-item checklist on paper.

00:01:01.459 --> 00:01:03.750 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will keep every secret off that page.

00:01:04.757 --> 00:01:06.602 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will mark the page Example so

00:01:06.602 --> 00:01:08.334 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
nobody can read it as an order.

00:01:09.442 --> 00:01:11.606 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The seven items are: a notebook,

00:01:11.606 --> 00:01:14.030 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
three words, range, levels and stop,

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:16.280 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the pair, paper or a demo account,

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:18.358 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
no secrets, a written stop, and

00:01:18.358 --> 00:01:20.695 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the word Example on every figure.

00:01:21.215 --> 00:01:22.596 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Each item has a reason.

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:24.457 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The notebook is the plan

00:01:24.457 --> 00:01:25.574 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you can check later.

00:01:25.827 --> 00:01:27.167 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The three words stop you

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:28.788 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
drawing a grid with no edges.

00:01:29.157 --> 00:01:30.442 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The pair names what you

00:01:30.442 --> 00:01:31.895 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
buy and what you pay with.

00:01:32.269 --> 00:01:33.733 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper or a demo is learner

00:01:33.733 --> 00:01:35.267 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
plates, or training wheels.

00:01:35.787 --> 00:01:37.966 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No secrets keeps the keys off the page.

00:01:38.458 --> 00:01:40.190 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The written stop is the action.

00:01:40.483 --> 00:01:42.271 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Example marks a teaching number.

00:01:42.681 --> 00:01:44.190 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For this course the pair is

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:45.828 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin priced in US dollars.

00:01:46.348 --> 00:01:48.541 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A demo account uses pretend money.

00:01:49.061 --> 00:01:50.677 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A daily close is the last

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:51.627 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price of the day.

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:53.572 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You are naming that public

00:01:53.572 --> 00:01:55.137 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
series, not choosing an app.

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:57.680 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Three words, before any number.

00:01:58.086 --> 00:02:00.670 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:03.215 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An order is an instruction to buy

00:02:03.215 --> 00:02:05.164 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
or sell that can wait for a price.

00:02:05.684 --> 00:02:08.050 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Levels are the price lines where orders

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:10.117 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
wait, like the rungs of a ladder, and

00:02:10.117 --> 00:02:12.296 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap is the space between two of them.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:15.078 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stop is the rule for what you will do if

00:02:15.078 --> 00:02:17.758 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a daily close finishes outside the range

00:02:17.758 --> 00:02:20.438 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the next daily close is still outside.

00:02:20.958 --> 00:02:22.779 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The figures from lesson 1 are

00:02:22.779 --> 00:02:24.448 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
on the card, marked Example.

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:26.644 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If you can only say one of the

00:02:26.644 --> 00:02:28.878 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
three words, the page is missing a part.

00:02:29.748 --> 00:02:31.871 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A wallet is where your crypto is held.

00:02:32.188 --> 00:02:34.087 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A seed phrase is the list of words

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:35.494 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that unlocks that wallet.

00:02:36.014 --> 00:02:37.411 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A private key is a secret

00:02:37.411 --> 00:02:38.878 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that can move your crypto.

00:02:39.398 --> 00:02:42.576 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An API secret is a password that lets

00:02:42.576 --> 00:02:44.919 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a program place orders on an account,

00:02:44.919 --> 00:02:47.105 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and sometimes move money out of it.

00:02:47.625 --> 00:02:50.252 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You never type a seed phrase, a private

00:02:50.252 --> 00:02:53.441 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
key, or an API secret onto this page.

00:02:53.961 --> 00:02:55.760 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The chart has no balance on it.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.401 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A public close is not your account.

00:02:58.921 --> 00:03:00.552 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a form asks for a secret,

00:03:00.552 --> 00:03:02.338 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that form is not this lesson.

00:03:03.388 --> 00:03:05.362 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You copy the range onto the page,

00:03:05.362 --> 00:03:06.804 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not every day's prices.

00:03:07.324 --> 00:03:09.558 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Copy the bottom line and the top

00:03:09.558 --> 00:03:11.706 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
line, with six gaps of about 900.

00:03:12.226 --> 00:03:13.847 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every close in that window

00:03:13.847 --> 00:03:15.187 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stayed inside the range.

00:03:15.681 --> 00:03:17.083 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Mark each figure Example.

00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:19.750 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Worked check: pair, range,

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:21.205 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
gaps, stop, and Example.

00:03:21.724 --> 00:03:23.939 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the stop line is only a tick with no

00:03:23.939 --> 00:03:26.006 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
sentence, the page fails the check.

00:03:26.526 --> 00:03:28.310 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The rule has to say: if a daily

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.646 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
close finishes outside the range

00:03:30.646 --> 00:03:32.904 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the next daily close is still

00:03:32.904 --> 00:03:34.688 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
outside, the example is over.

00:03:35.738 --> 00:03:37.749 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A page is the notebook you can hold.

00:03:38.245 --> 00:03:40.206 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange is the app or website

00:03:40.206 --> 00:03:42.167 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
where people buy and sell crypto.

00:03:42.687 --> 00:03:44.196 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The screen is the exchange.

00:03:44.626 --> 00:03:46.149 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 1 ended by asking

00:03:46.149 --> 00:03:47.444 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you to bring the page.

00:03:47.964 --> 00:03:49.360 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This lesson is that page.

00:03:49.875 --> 00:03:51.886 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Open the notebook before any screen.

00:03:52.797 --> 00:03:54.864 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write today's date on the first line.

00:03:55.213 --> 00:03:57.057 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Under it, write the word Example.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:58.919 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Example means a real past

00:03:58.919 --> 00:04:00.327 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price used for practice.

00:04:00.847 --> 00:04:02.970 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not an order and not a forecast.

00:04:04.095 --> 00:04:05.268 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write the pair first.

00:04:05.672 --> 00:04:07.069 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The base is what you buy.

00:04:07.569 --> 00:04:09.301 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The quote is what you pay with.

00:04:09.635 --> 00:04:12.827 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For this course the prices are the July

00:04:12.827 --> 00:04:15.918 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to October example window, the public

00:04:15.918 --> 00:04:18.611 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin closes from 19 July to 16

00:04:18.611 --> 00:04:21.204 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
October 2023, so you buy the base,

00:04:21.204 --> 00:04:23.996 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin, with the quote, US dollars,

00:04:23.996 --> 00:04:26.689 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and that row is labelled BTC/USD.

00:04:27.209 --> 00:04:29.220 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every other row depends on the pair.

00:04:29.442 --> 00:04:31.023 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
We price in US dollars.

00:04:31.543 --> 00:04:33.295 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Your exchange may charge fees

00:04:33.295 --> 00:04:34.767 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in Australian dollars, so

00:04:34.767 --> 00:04:36.331 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
keep each in its own column.

00:04:36.829 --> 00:04:39.005 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a fee sum is in Australian

00:04:39.005 --> 00:04:41.181 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars, that sum goes on its

00:04:41.181 --> 00:04:43.262 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
own line, labelled BTC/AUD.

00:04:43.782 --> 00:04:45.688 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Do not put a US dollar price and

00:04:45.688 --> 00:04:48.205 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
an Australian dollar fee on the same row.

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:51.839 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

00:04:52.595 --> 00:04:57.077 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In the July to October example window

00:04:57.574 --> 00:05:00.761 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
those lines are 24,930 and 30,331.

00:05:01.281 --> 00:05:02.677 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Both figures are Example.

00:05:03.181 --> 00:05:05.080 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Levels are the lines between them.

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:07.529 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Six gaps of about 900 dollars sit

00:05:07.529 --> 00:05:09.528 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
between the top and the bottom.

00:05:10.048 --> 00:05:11.903 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write the top and the bottom only

00:05:11.903 --> 00:05:13.914 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
after you have said what a range is.

00:05:14.348 --> 00:05:16.238 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then write one gap, and how you

00:05:16.238 --> 00:05:18.206 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
got it: the top minus the bottom,

00:05:18.206 --> 00:05:20.096 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
divided by the number of gaps.

00:05:21.146 --> 00:05:22.417 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The stop sentence has

00:05:22.417 --> 00:05:23.757 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to say what you will do.

00:05:24.207 --> 00:05:26.015 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A bot is a program that places

00:05:26.015 --> 00:05:28.424 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and cancels the waiting orders for you.

00:05:28.944 --> 00:05:31.067 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Two daily closes outside the range,

00:05:31.067 --> 00:05:32.823 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
through the top or the bottom,

00:05:32.823 --> 00:05:35.132 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the second close still outside.

00:05:35.652 --> 00:05:37.216 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then you stop the bot, which

00:05:37.216 --> 00:05:38.804 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cancels the waiting orders,

00:05:38.804 --> 00:05:40.704 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and you follow the rule you wrote.

00:05:41.216 --> 00:05:43.003 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write that stop in one sentence.

00:05:43.965 --> 00:05:46.695 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A deposit is crypto or Australian dollars

00:05:46.695 --> 00:05:49.192 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you send into an account at an exchange.

00:05:49.712 --> 00:05:51.728 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange in Australia asks who

00:05:51.728 --> 00:05:53.528 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you are before you can deposit.

00:05:54.048 --> 00:05:56.351 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That check is required by Australian

00:05:56.351 --> 00:05:58.283 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
anti-money laundering law, and

00:05:58.283 --> 00:06:00.511 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the exchange runs it, not this course.

00:06:01.031 --> 00:06:03.035 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You only upload identification

00:06:03.035 --> 00:06:04.890 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
inside the exchange's own app.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:07.477 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This course does not name an exchange

00:06:07.477 --> 00:06:09.041 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and does not show a balance.

00:06:09.302 --> 00:06:11.844 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Any exchange offering crypto services

00:06:11.844 --> 00:06:14.463 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in Australia must register with AUSTRAC,

00:06:14.463 --> 00:06:17.083 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australia's financial crime regulator,

00:06:17.083 --> 00:06:19.394 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
as a virtual asset service provider.

00:06:19.914 --> 00:06:21.178 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
AUSTRAC keeps a public

00:06:21.178 --> 00:06:22.519 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
register you can search.

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:25.208 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check that register before you sign up.

00:06:25.681 --> 00:06:27.972 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The register says the business is listed.

00:06:28.399 --> 00:06:30.633 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It does not say your money is protected.

00:06:30.913 --> 00:06:33.508 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Registration is not a safety guarantee.

00:06:34.028 --> 00:06:36.159 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
ASIC is Australia's financial

00:06:36.159 --> 00:06:37.390 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
services regulator.

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:40.814 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
From April 2027, platforms that hold

00:06:40.814 --> 00:06:43.772 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
crypto for you need an ASIC licence,

00:06:43.772 --> 00:06:46.676 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with a transition period to October

00:06:46.676 --> 00:06:49.774 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
2027 for platforms already operating.

00:06:50.294 --> 00:06:52.305 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check ASIC for the current position.

00:06:52.756 --> 00:06:54.736 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This lesson names only government

00:06:54.736 --> 00:06:56.189 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bodies, never an exchange.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:58.896 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A second code, as well as your

00:06:58.896 --> 00:07:01.335 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
password, is two-factor authentication.

00:07:01.855 --> 00:07:03.955 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Turn that on before any real dollars.

00:07:04.475 --> 00:07:06.508 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then look for a paper or demo mode.

00:07:07.094 --> 00:07:08.616 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper uses pretend money.

00:07:09.136 --> 00:07:10.756 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That practice is lesson 7.

00:07:11.806 --> 00:07:13.315 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A fill is when your waiting

00:07:13.315 --> 00:07:14.602 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
order actually trades.

00:07:15.122 --> 00:07:17.412 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A maker fee is the charge when your order

00:07:17.412 --> 00:07:19.535 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
waits and someone else trades with it.

00:07:19.745 --> 00:07:21.421 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A taker fee is the charge when

00:07:21.421 --> 00:07:23.153 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your order fills straight away.

00:07:23.489 --> 00:07:25.188 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid uses waiting orders,

00:07:25.188 --> 00:07:26.886 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so read the maker fee first.

00:07:27.406 --> 00:07:28.859 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Some bots also pay a taker

00:07:28.859 --> 00:07:30.311 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
fee when they first start.

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:33.543 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In this example both are 0.1 percent.

00:07:34.063 --> 00:07:37.142 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On an example buy of 100 Australian

00:07:37.142 --> 00:07:39.903 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars, 0.1 percent is 10 cents.

00:07:40.423 --> 00:07:42.546 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The sell costs about 10 cents as well.

00:07:42.868 --> 00:07:44.712 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The round trip is about 20

00:07:44.712 --> 00:07:46.644 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cents, which is 0.2 percent.

00:07:47.164 --> 00:07:49.201 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This fee row is Australian dollars.

00:07:49.721 --> 00:07:50.784 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not the July

00:07:50.784 --> 00:07:52.454 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to October example window.

00:07:52.974 --> 00:07:55.285 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the gap is smaller than that 0.2

00:07:55.285 --> 00:07:57.762 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
percent, each completed buy and sell

00:07:57.762 --> 00:08:00.403 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
costs more in fees than the gap is worth.

00:08:00.923 --> 00:08:02.878 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
To compare them, turn the gap into

00:08:02.878 --> 00:08:05.050 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a percent by dividing it by the price.

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:08.567 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In the lesson 1 example, 900

00:08:08.567 --> 00:08:11.973 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
divided by 27,630 is about 3.3

00:08:11.973 --> 00:08:15.515 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
percent, well above 0.2 percent.

00:08:16.035 --> 00:08:17.579 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 5 is where you test

00:08:17.579 --> 00:08:18.903 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap against this fee.

00:08:19.423 --> 00:08:21.490 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not pick a gap in this lesson.

00:08:22.122 --> 00:08:24.290 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stablecoin is a coin built

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:26.504 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to stay worth about one US dollar.

00:08:27.024 --> 00:08:28.644 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It can still lose that value.

00:08:29.113 --> 00:08:31.566 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If your pair is priced in a stablecoin,

00:08:31.566 --> 00:08:34.392 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
every fill trades one coin for another,

00:08:34.392 --> 00:08:35.816 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so every fill is a swap.

00:08:36.866 --> 00:08:39.072 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A trading journal is a dated record

00:08:39.072 --> 00:08:40.364 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
of every bot: the plan,

00:08:40.364 --> 00:08:42.265 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the changes, the fills, the fees,

00:08:42.265 --> 00:08:44.166 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a review note of what happened,

00:08:44.166 --> 00:08:46.372 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and whether you followed the rules.

00:08:46.892 --> 00:08:48.679 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That note is not money you made.

00:08:49.028 --> 00:08:51.163 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stablecoin fill goes in the journal.

00:08:51.683 --> 00:08:53.995 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The tax office treats a swap like a sale,

00:08:53.995 --> 00:08:55.945 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so every swap goes in the journal.

00:08:56.465 --> 00:08:58.750 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The journal is also the page you will

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:00.959 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
open again in lesson 8 and lesson 10.

00:09:01.479 --> 00:09:04.005 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For every transaction, including a buy,

00:09:04.005 --> 00:09:06.057 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a sell, a swap, or a transfer, write

00:09:06.057 --> 00:09:08.503 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the date and time, the amount, the value

00:09:08.503 --> 00:09:10.713 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in Australian dollars at the time,

00:09:10.713 --> 00:09:13.160 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the fee, which exchange or wallet, what

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:15.448 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
it was for, and who the other side was.

00:09:15.968 --> 00:09:18.042 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The columns are the date, the pair,

00:09:18.042 --> 00:09:19.809 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the range, the gaps, the money

00:09:19.809 --> 00:09:21.269 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in the bot, the stop rule,

00:09:21.269 --> 00:09:23.420 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the fills, the fees, the Australian

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:25.571 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollar value of each fill, a review

00:09:25.571 --> 00:09:27.582 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
note, and a yes or no for the rules.

00:09:28.088 --> 00:09:29.725 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The Australian dollar value

00:09:29.725 --> 00:09:31.294 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
column is the one exception.

00:09:31.814 --> 00:09:33.322 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is for your tax records.

00:09:33.839 --> 00:09:35.943 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Download your exchange's transaction

00:09:35.943 --> 00:09:37.954 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
history at least every three months.

00:09:38.375 --> 00:09:39.380 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Keep those records

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:40.721 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for at least five years.

00:09:41.078 --> 00:09:42.850 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information,

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:43.736 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not tax advice.

00:09:44.256 --> 00:09:46.043 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Leave two columns blank for now.

00:09:46.463 --> 00:09:47.626 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One is for the fees.

00:09:48.146 --> 00:09:50.436 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One is for whether you followed the rule.

00:09:50.571 --> 00:09:51.744 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You fill those later.

00:09:52.193 --> 00:09:54.036 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not fill them with a hope.

00:09:54.697 --> 00:09:56.947 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Nobody from this course will ask

00:09:56.947 --> 00:09:58.780 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for a seed phrase, a private

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:00.934 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
key, or an API secret.

00:10:01.454 --> 00:10:03.430 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a message rushes you to send

00:10:03.430 --> 00:10:04.852 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
crypto, or asks for one

00:10:04.852 --> 00:10:06.512 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
of those, treat it as a scam.

00:10:07.032 --> 00:10:08.261 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not this course.

00:10:09.274 --> 00:10:11.876 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
ASIC's Moneysmart website is the public

00:10:11.876 --> 00:10:14.039 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australian guide for scam warnings.

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:15.565 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check it yourself.

00:10:16.556 --> 00:10:18.552 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Now cover the chart and say your

00:10:18.552 --> 00:10:20.548 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
page out loud: the pair, the range,

00:10:20.548 --> 00:10:22.161 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the gaps and the stop rule.

00:10:22.681 --> 00:10:24.682 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Name the pair, the range, the gaps,

00:10:24.682 --> 00:10:26.375 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the stop rule, then stop.

00:10:26.895 --> 00:10:29.015 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a word on it has not been defined,

00:10:29.015 --> 00:10:31.135 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stop and define it before you go on.

00:10:31.655 --> 00:10:33.485 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A secret is a seed phrase,

00:10:33.485 --> 00:10:36.477 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a private key, or an API secret.

00:10:36.997 --> 00:10:38.673 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
None of those go on this page.

00:10:39.072 --> 00:10:40.750 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You write Example on your own

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:42.637 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
notebook so a practice sketch is

00:10:42.637 --> 00:10:44.735 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
never later mistaken for a live plan.

00:10:45.785 --> 00:10:48.165 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Recap: your page has seven items, each

00:10:48.165 --> 00:10:50.306 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with a written fact, every figure

00:10:50.306 --> 00:10:52.606 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
marked Example, and no secrets on it.

00:10:53.806 --> 00:10:55.220 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson: How a grid

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:56.792 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bot works, order by order.

00:10:57.312 --> 00:10:58.932 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Bring your notes: your range,

00:10:58.932 --> 00:11:00.552 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your gaps and your stop rule.

00:11:00.794 --> 00:11:02.151 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Keep the word Example on

00:11:02.151 --> 00:11:03.441 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
every practice figure.

00:11:03.961 --> 00:11:05.609 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson you will see what

00:11:05.609 --> 00:11:08.167 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the bot does, order by order.

